 Neural Stochastic Differential Equations
The Neural SDE takes the form
yt = lθ(xt),
dxt = μθ(t, xt)dt + σθ(t, xt)dWt ,
x0 ∼ νθ(ξ),
where • μθ, σθ and νθ are neural networks.
• lθ is a linear map.
• W is a multidimensional Brownian motion.
• ξ ∼ N (0, Id) is some initial noise.
